Z||000002||mwbackus||03-12-2000||04:18 AM||||According to my calculations, it is approx. $400 more than a V8archie kit with the same components (excluding axle shafts).<P><BR>HTD  -       $2300<P><BR>V8 Archie<P>Deluxe Kit   $1550<BR>Clutch       $ 350<BR>___________________<BR>             $1900<P>To compare the master V8archie kit to this copy of a Zumalt kit is not a fair comparison.  The master kit is much more complete, it includes all of the small parts that are needed(ie..fittings, clamps, hoses, belts, etc.).<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||03-12-2000||01:30 PM||||If this is a copy of the Zumalt kit, then it centers the motor in the cradle? This is a good thing, right? With this kit, you can run a factory style water pump? For these reasons alone, it may be worth the extra $400. Comments?||||reg||3
